Requirement {{id}} (rev {{rev}}, stage={{stage}}): {{title}}
Description: {{desc}}
Mandatory references: read docs/README.md (wiki index) first, then docs/context/* (domain invariants) and docs/design/* (architecture & contracts) before proposing or editing.
Worktree: {{worktree}} (branch={{branch}}, base={{base}})
Artifact: {{artifact}} — deliver through the harness archive, never as a stray file in a checkout: return the full content in your final report (or write it under /tmp) and the main session records it into the run archive with `--artifact-put artifacts/<name>.md`. All artifacts of a run live only in that run's archive (`<run-dir>/artifacts/`); do not write artifact files into any checkout's `artifacts/` — that path is a git-ignored scratch area, not the authoritative copy.
Submit: {{submit}}
Integration (development stage only): at closeout you integrate your feature branch into `develop` yourself — align `origin/develop`, `git merge --no-ff`, integrated-state gates green, push `develop`, and record the develop merge SHA (`develop@<sha>`) in the artifact. Never touch `master` or another lane's branch.
Doc sync (when applicable): the docs wiki — docs/README.md (index) with docs/context/* (domain vocabulary, principles, decision ledger) and docs/design/* (system behaviour, interface contracts) — is the always-current authority of the whole repository — never a changelog, history lives in git and settlement artifacts. If your change alters how any subsystem works or is meant to work (kernel crates / egg CLI / Mod / serve / tooling): at the plan stage declare in your artifact which wiki files it touches; at the development stage update those files in place on your feature branch (decisions/vocabulary -> the matching decisions-*/vocabulary entry in docs/context/ for the D-MAx in this brief; behaviour/contracts -> the matching docs/design/ chapter for that subsystem). Pure fixes and rewording touch neither.
